# THE DEMO IS A SECOND SPA, MOUNTED AT /demo/, and it needs its own
# fallback: the root one below would hand it the product's index.html,
# which boots with no basename and lands on the landing page.
#
# The destination is /demo-shell.html and NOT /demo/index.html, which is
# what it used to be. That old destination matches its own source
# pattern, and a self-referencing rewrite is the most likely reason the
# rule was silently dropped on Cloudflare Pages — /demo/ worked (a real
# file) while every deep link under it fell through to the rule below.
#
# This rule is now the SECOND line of defence. The demo build writes a
# real .html file for every route the router declares (see
# demoRouteShells in vite.config.js), and a static asset is served before
# any of this is consulted. What is left for this rule is a /demo/ URL
# that matches no declared route.
/demo/*  /demo-shell.html  200

# The product, at the root, where the host's own fallback would do the
# same job. Stated anyway so the behaviour is in the repository rather
# than in a dashboard setting.
/*       /index.html       200
